 Grumps call us, are a semi-Court of those Changelings who can incorporate the old ways into the new. We're more like a mix of a Elks' Club and a speak-easy, not out to take over the world, but doesn't fear bringing change to the people, mortal or Changeling. It's a loose collaboration to keep the spark of imagination alive in this new age and stay off the Banality that consumes it. Within the &quot;Lodge&quot; (for lack of a better term), have several factions depending on which artistic medium we prefer. The Director's Chair are those who are adapt at film and television, are Changelings adapt at bringing the spark through various films and tv shows. The Acting Troupe are exactly as you think they are, actors. From theater, to television, and film; they are the largest chapter of the Netweavers, with both numbers and the experience to boot. The Quill are the authors, fan-fiction and blogs, the written word, novellas and novels, screen plays and scripts, they are the second oldest of the Netweavers utilizing the power of the printing press to the internet, and keep a vast wealth of imagination. The Bardic Troupe are the musicians and music producers. The Bards are the oldest chapter, with various skills from instruments, to singing, song writing, even radio djs fall under this chapter. They also suffer the most Banality since music is just as harsh if not more so than film and television. And finally the founders of the &quot;Court&quot; The Netweavers themselves. They use the internet to bring imagination to a very wide audience. Videos, blogs and vlogs, podcasts, they are the most neutral per say of all the chapters. I do mean per say cause there's stiff competition between the chapters themselves, all be it friendly competition. About the most that gets damaged between the chapters are just one's pride. Even then it's minor bruising when one of the chapters has a hit before the others.</i><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Onyx Path Kickstarters 