delines, and small enough so it hasn't been found by the Seelie Courts or other authorities.<br /> <br /> Unseelie of The Quill are dying out, but still have a foothold in pornography. One magazine that still remains is The Satyr. It's very close to breaking not only the &quot;Golden rule&quot; as I've heard of the variations from other supernaturals; No Mortal should know we exist. But also the contents inside would bring charges of not only the person who bought the magazine, but those who have participated for their &quot;big shot&quot;. Unseelie rapists ravenge the participants, and there's rumor of Formorian children from the unfortunate women who got pregnant from their photo shoots. The Unseelie Bards are the weakest of the chapters. They are more of the trash and heavy metal types. Some within the Unseelie Netweavers would call them tame. But with Unseelie music, it's the slowest to affect mortals. Remember the trials in the eighties that hair metal music is the Devil's work and it's affecting the youth of the time, that was the Unseelie Bards hayday. Some rements pop up from time to time, mostly the leftover Formorians and renegades. The Unseelie Netweavers are what you would expect of the modern age. True Trolz, as the internet spelling implies. Slut Shammers, forum Trolls, hyper judgmental cynics. Their main haunts on the internet is a site call Ch4ntz, Jezuztranzmitionz, and Dave's Ads. While the first two should be avoided if you don't want to feel your brain cells atomically explode, Dave's Ads you should not go or respond. All sorts of Unseelie prowl the Ads for fresh victims, in whatever way they want. Recruiters from Hacksville/Horndog and The Satyr place their recruitment advertisements on the Ads to seek &quot;upcoming actors&quot;, &quot;girls who like attention&quot;, and the ever classic &quot;need quick cash&quot;. Many who respond to the posts are never heard from again, depending on the post, your last known images would cost $19.95 S+H.</i>